---
/**
 * Studies index.
 *
 * Ordered as a progression rather than as a catalogue: each study exists because the one
 * before it left something unestablished, and the index says so. Within a stage the entry
 * for a completed case carries four things and nothing else -- the question it asked, what
 * it found, whether its evidence ships, and a link. The methodological description that
 * used to sit here is on each case page, which is the only place it can be read next to
 * the evidence it describes.
 *
 * A2 is listed as unavailable rather than as a study a reader could reproduce. Future
 * stages are set back so they cannot be mistaken for results.
 */
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Callout from "../../components/Callout.astro";
import StatusTable from "../../components/StatusTable.astro";
import { baseScenario } from "../../scripts/scenarios";
import { NAV } from "../../scripts/site";
import { href } from "../../lib/urls";

const base = await baseScenario();

const contents = [
  { id: "stage-a", label: "Stage A — inventory" },
  { id: "stage-b", label: "Stage B — transient" },
  { id: "unavailable", label: "Not available publicly" },
  { id: "status", label: "Status at a glance" },
  { id: "roadmap", label: "Not yet done" },
];

const description =
  "Six synthetic studies in two stages: A1, A3 and A4 on inventory and material balance, and B1 and B2 on pressure-transient interpretation. Each exists because the one before it left something unestablished.";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Studies"
  description={description}
  canonicalPath="/studies/"
  nav={NAV}
  contents={contents}
>
  <h1>Studies</h1>

  <p class="lede">
    Two stages, five studies. Each one exists because the one before it left something
    unestablished, and both stages end the same way: with a case where the answer looks
    convincing and is wrong.
  </p>

  <section id="stage-a" aria-labelledby="stage-a-h">
    <h2 id="stage-a-h">Stage A — inventory and material balance</h2>

    <ol class="track">
      <li class="track__item">
        <p class="track__role">Establish the instrument</p>
        <h3><a href={href("/studies/a1/")}>A1 — the exact recovery, and how narrow &ldquo;exact&rdquo; is</a></h3>
        <p class="track__q">Does the p/Z inverse recover a known gas in place from noise-free data?</p>
        <p class="track__a">
          Exactly — and a seeded-defect check shows a whole class of errors leaves the
          recovered inventory unchanged, so the exact recovery is evidence only against the
          defects the design can see.
        </p>
        <p class="track__status">Reproduces byte for byte in the canonical environment.</p>
      </li>

      <li class="track__item">
        <p class="track__role">Understand its uncertainty</p>
        <h3><a href={href("/studies/a3/")}>A3 — the error budget that re-ranks itself</a></h3>
        <p class="track__q">Which measurement error dominates the inferred gas in place?</p>
        <p class="track__a">
          Random pressure scatter, at 1.32 percent of G — but the ranking reverses when the
          assumed gauge accuracy is halved. That reversal was pre-registered as an inconclusive
          condition, and it triggered.
        </p>
        <p class="track__status">Reproduces byte for byte. Ordinate-side only.</p>
      </li>

      <li class="track__item track__item--flagship">
        <p class="track__role">Show it failing while looking convincing</p>
        <h3><a href={href("/studies/a4/")}>A4 — when a straight p/Z line is convincing and wrong</a></h3>
        <p class="track__q">
          If an aquifer supports the reservoir, how wrong is the volumetric answer and would
          anyone be able to tell from the data?
        </p>
        <p class="track__a">
          R-squared = {base.rSquared.toFixed(6)} and the inventory is
          {" "}{base.errorPct.toFixed(1)} percent too high. Over most of the range the quality of
          the fit does not indicate the size of the error.
        </p>
        <p class="track__status">
          Reproduces byte for byte. Nine exhibits, eight computed aquifer strengths, a decision
          memo and a measured detection-power curve.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section id="stage-b" aria-labelledby="stage-b-h">
    <h2 id="stage-b-h">Stage B — transient interpretation</h2>

    <ol class="track">
      <li class="track__item track__item--flagship">
        <p class="track__role">Establish a second instrument, then attack it</p>
        <h3><a href={href("/studies/b1/")}>B1 — a correct interpretation can still be wrong when its inputs are wrong</a></h3>
        <p class="track__q">
          Can a semilog interpretation recover a known permeability and skin, and what still
          makes a convincing interpretation wrong once it can?
        </p>
        <p class="track__a">
          It recovers them essentially exactly. Then five of ten seeded analyst errors put a
          reported number materially wrong while moving no diagnostic at all.
        </p>
        <p class="track__status">
          Reproduces byte for byte. Nine pre-registered criteria: eight recorded as flags in the
          run, and determinism verified by re-running and diffing. Wellbore storage is zero by
          declared design.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li class="track__item track__item--flagship">
        <p class="track__role">Take the window away and see whether the rule can find it</p>
        <h3><a href={href("/studies/b2/")}>B2 — an accurate answer can exist before the test can certify it</a></h3>
        <p class="track__q">
          B1 was handed its interpretation window. Can a declared, truth-blind rule find the
          radial-flow interval itself, in a drawdown that begins under wellbore storage?
        </p>
        <p class="track__a">
          On its own primary case it declined. Measured afterwards against the hidden truth,
          1.6 decades of adequate data were present and 1 decade was required — and the record
          certified none of it.
        </p>
        <p class="track__status">
          Classified INCONCLUSIVE by the frozen protocol, which is a valid outcome under it.
          Every verification criterion met; window detection on the primary case failed and no
          threshold was changed. Across 800 noisy replicates the rule produced no false
          acceptance.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section id="unavailable" aria-labelledby="unavailable-h">
    <h2 id="unavailable-h">Not available in the public profile</h2>

    <div class="track__item track__item--unavailable">
      <p class="track__role">Compare against values this project did not produce</p>
      <h3><a href={href("/studies/a2/")}>A2 — independent PVT check</a></h3>
      <p class="track__q">
        Do the deviation-factor and viscosity correlations agree with laboratory-grade
        reference equations of state?
      </p>
      <p class="track__a">
        Unknown here. A2 is the only study that compares the code against values it did not
        produce, and the only one whose inputs this repository cannot redistribute.
      </p>
      <p class="track__status">
        <strong>No figure, no table and no number from A2 appears on this site.</strong> Its run
        script exits non-zero when the reference extract is absent rather than producing a
        result from nothing.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="status" aria-labelledby="status-h">
    <h2 id="status-h">Status at a glance</h2>

    <StatusTable
      caption="What each study ships in the public profile, and where that was established."
      captionTitle="Studies"
      rows={[
        {
          check: "A4 — misleading fit counterexample",
          scope: "Nine exhibits, eight computed aquifer cases, decision memo",
          environment: "CPython 3.13.2 on the author's machine, 2026-09-13",
          state: "PASS",
          note: "re-run into a fresh directory and, in the canonical environment, diffed byte for byte against the committed snapshot",
          evidence: { label: "Case page", path: "/studies/a4/" },
        },
        {
          check: "A1 — volumetric baseline",
          scope: "Numerical verification of the p/Z inverse, plus two post-hoc diagnostics",
          environment: "CPython 3.13.2 on the author's machine, 2026-09-13",
          state: "PASS",
          note: "byte-identical on re-run; D1 and D2 are not pre-registered and not gated",
          evidence: { label: "Case page", path: "/studies/a1/" },
        },
        {
          check: "A3 — uncertainty experiments",
          scope: "Ordinate-side measurement error budget on a synthetic closed tank",
          environment: "CPython 3.13.2 on the author's machine, 2026-09-13",
          state: "PASS",
          note: "byte-identical on re-run; one pre-registered inconclusive condition triggered and is reported as inconclusive",
          evidence: { label: "Case page", path: "/studies/a3/" },
        },
        {
          check: "A2 — independent PVT check",
          scope: "Correlations against laboratory-grade reference equations of state",
          environment: "not run anywhere in the public profile",
          state: "BLOCKED",
          note: "its reference inputs are not redistributed; the run script exits 1 when they are absent",
          evidence: { label: "Availability page", path: "/studies/a2/" },
        },
        {
          check: "B1 — infinite-acting radial flow",
          scope: "Recovery of a known permeability and skin, plus a seeded-defect visibility diagnostic",
          environment: "digest-pinned Linux container, reproduced on four further environments",
          state: "PASS",
          note: "9 of 9 pre-registered criteria: 8 recorded as flags in the run, and determinism verified by re-running and diffing. The negative control fails as required; the defect-visibility diagnostic is post-hoc and not gated",
          evidence: { label: "Case page", path: "/studies/b1/" },
        },
        {
          check: "B2 — wellbore storage and the radial window",
          scope: "Whether the case runs, reproduces byte for byte, and satisfies the verification criteria frozen before it ran",
          environment: "digest-pinned Linux container, reproduced on four further environments",
          state: "PASS",
          note: "the scientific classification is INCONCLUSIVE, which is a valid outcome of the frozen protocol and not a failing check: every verification criterion is met, while window detection on the primary case failed and no threshold was changed. The post-hoc duration analysis is reported separately and gates nothing",
          evidence: { label: "Case page", path: "/studies/b2/" },
        },
        {
          check: "Hosted continuous integration",
          scope: "The suite, canonical reproduction and cross-platform portability, run off the author's machine",
          environment: "GitHub-hosted runners: three CPython versions, one pinned container, four portability environments",
          state: "PASS",
          note: "green, and it is still this repository testing itself rather than external validation",
          evidence: { label: "Methods", path: "/methods/" },
        },
        {
          check: "Human peer review",
          scope: "Review by a person other than the author",
          environment: "not run anywhere",
          state: "NOT RUN",
          note: "every review pass was conducted under a different role by the same author",
          evidence: { label: "About", path: "/about/" },
        },
      ]}
      id="studies-status"
    />
  </section>

  <section id="roadmap" aria-labelledby="roadmap-h">
    <h2 id="roadmap-h">Not yet done</h2>

    <Callout kind="note" title="This is future work, not results">
      <p>
        Nothing in this section has been run. It is listed so that a reader can see what the
        project intends and can tell it apart from what it has actually produced. None of it
        has a figure, a number or a study page.
      </p>
    </Callout>

    <ul class="future">
      <li>
        <strong>B3 through B6.</strong> Build-up and superposition; boundaries; real-gas
        pseudopressure and pseudotime; and a case against data this project did not generate.
        B2, which closed B1's largest gap by taking the interpretation window away, has been
        run and its result is on its own page.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Stage C and Stage D.</strong> Not started, and not scoped beyond a heading.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>The abscissa.</strong> A3's own recommendation, and the one gap it says it is
        least able to defend: put a metering bias and a random metering error through the
        existing machinery so the error budget covers the volume axis as well as the pressure
        axis.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>A companion diagnostic case for A4.</strong> Pre-register a test of the
        fitted-versus-measured initial p/Z mismatch and of the Cole plot's power against the
        same noise sweep, with the deviation-factor correlation mismatched between generator
        and analyst, and with an independent seed per noise level.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <style>
    .lede {
      max-width: 54ch;
    }

    .track {
      list-style: none;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      display: grid;
      gap: var(--space-8);
    }

    /* A study is a passage of prose with a role above it, not a card. The only rule is a
       hairline on the inline edge, which carries the sense of a sequence. */
    .track__item {
      padding-inline-start: var(--space-5);
      border-inline-start: 2px solid var(--c-rule);
      max-width: var(--prose-max);
    }

    .track__item--flagship {
      border-inline-start-color: var(--c-ink);
    }

    .track__item--unavailable {
      border-inline-start-style: dashed;
      max-width: var(--prose-max);
      padding-inline-start: var(--space-5);
      border-inline-start-width: 2px;
      border-inline-start-color: var(--c-border-strong);
    }

    .track__role {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: var(--text-xs);
      letter-spacing: 0.06em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--c-ink-3);
      font-weight: 600;
    }

    .track__item h3 {
      margin-block: var(--space-2) var(--space-3);
      font-size: var(--text-lg);
      line-height: 1.3;
    }

    .track__item h3 a {
      color: var(--c-ink);
    }

    .track__item h3 a:hover,
    .track__item h3 a:focus-visible {
      color: var(--c-blue-strong);
    }

    .track__q {
      color: var(--c-ink-2);
    }

    .track__a {
      color: var(--c-ink);
    }

    .track__status {
      font-size: var(--text-sm);
      color: var(--c-ink-3);
      margin-block-end: 0;
    }

    .future {
      max-width: var(--prose-max);
      color: var(--c-ink-2);
    }

    .future li {
      margin-block: var(--space-4);
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
